    "api_version": "2026-07",
    "retrieved": "2026-09-01",
    "derivation": "Hand-authored per D21. The ORDERS_FULFILLED sample's top-level key set was diffed against ORDERS_PAID and found IDENTICAL — zero keys differ — so this recording reuses that key set and differs only in the fulfilment-bearing members. Values are invented. No live capture (D3).",
    "caveats": [
      "Shopify's own ORDERS_FULFILLED sample is not actually fulfilled: it shows fulfillment_status: null and fulfillments: []. So the published page gives NO element shape for a fulfilled order's fulfillments array.",
      "The seven-key fulfillment element below (created_at, id, order_id, status, tracking_company, tracking_number, updated_at) is the abbreviated form printed on the REST Order resource page. The standalone REST Fulfillment resource carries a much larger set, and which one a real webhook embeds is NOT DOCUMENTED. The stub emits exactly these seven rather than guessing at the larger shape.",
      "Everything in webhook_orders_paid.json's caveats applies here too; the top-level shape is the same object.",
      "documented_keys is INHERITED from webhook_orders_paid.json and then extended with the fulfillments[] element shape. That is not a shortcut: the two samples' top-level key sets were diffed and found identical, so maintaining a second hand-copied enumeration would only create an opportunity for the two to drift apart."
    ]
  },
